    "language": "en",
    "md5": "e12c732660df2af3cf5359766cbd58dc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1953,
    "chunk_text": "Even as the company expanded rapidly, financial discipline remained a priority. Net finance costs declined by 29% to Rs. 101 million, supported by prudent capital management and exchange gains generated through export growth.\n\nBehind this momentum is leadership with clarity of purpose. Executive Director and Chief Executive Officer Harsha Jayatunga has steered Sierra Cables through a period of transformation, positioning the company as a globally competitive manufacturer aligned with international standards. In doing so, he has acknowledged the role of Chairman Ishara Nanayakkara, whose strategic guidance and long-term vision continue to shape the organisation\u2019s direction.\n\nReflecting on the company\u2019s performance, Jayatunga noted that the results represent more than financial growth. They demonstrate the strength of a strategy built on uncompromising quality, global compliance standards and continuous innovation. The Sierra brand today stands recognised across international markets where technical credibility and consistency are essential.\n\nThat credibility has also been acknowledged by independent institutions. Fitch Ratings has continued to affirm Sierra Cables\u2019 A+ (lka) national long-term rating with a stable outlook. The rating reflects strong governance practices, consistent cash flow generation, prudent leverage management and a solid market position.\n\nIn global manufacturing, trust is earned through standards. Sierra Cables holds a distinction that no other Sri Lankan cable manufacturer can claim \u2014 certification to the UL 44 standard. This globally recognised certification confirms that Sierra\u2019s products meet the stringent safety and performance requirements demanded by highly regulated international markets. It is also the reason Sierra remains the only Sri Lankan cable manufacturer successfully supplying the United States market, widely regarded as one of the most demanding cable markets in the world."
  },
