    "md5": "8940c5660dfab12baa7561c79eb1f04e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1943,
    "chunk_text": "In global manufacturing, trust is earned through standards. Sierra Cables holds a distinction that no other Sri Lankan cable manufacturer can claim \u2014 certification to the UL 44 standard. This globally recognised certification confirms that Sierra\u2019s products meet the stringent safety and performance requirements demanded by highly regulated international markets. It is also the reason Sierra remains the only Sri Lankan cable manufacturer successfully supplying the United States market, widely regarded as one of the most demanding cable markets in the world.\n\nExport excellence has also been recognised formally. At the Export Awards organised by the National Chamber of Exporters of Sri Lanka, Sierra Cables was named Best Sri Lankan Brand Exporter and received the Gold Award in the Large Category under the Electronic and Electrical Products Sector. The recognition reflects the Company\u2019s manufacturing capabilities and its ability to consistently meet international quality requirements across multiple regions.\n\nSierra\u2019s growth trajectory is rooted in deliberate strategy. The Company has expanded its export portfolio by entering and sustaining business in demanding global markets while strengthening its dealer network across Sri Lanka to deepen domestic market presence. At the same time, it continues to invest in modern manufacturing technologies, automation and precision engineering to improve efficiency and reliability. Warehouse expansion currently underway further enhances logistics capabilities and ensures the organisation is equipped to respond to growing demand across both local and export markets.\n\nResearch and development are central to Sierra Cables\u2019 long-term vision. The company is introducing specialized cable solutions to meet evolving infrastructure and energy needs, including products for renewable energy systems and high-performance cables for modern construction and industrial applications."
