    "md5": "1062035034bb002f519c4563b7383607",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1914,
    "chunk_text": "\u2018Edges of Sri Lanka\u2019 to showcase country\u2019s unique exports value proposition\n\nEdges of Sri Lanka, a national branding initiative designed to articulate Sri Lanka\u2019s unique value proposition to global markets, was unveiled alongside the official launch of Sri Lanka Expo 2026 by the Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB), under the guidance of the Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Ministry.\n\nDeveloped in partnership with the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka (BOI) and the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce, with Deloitte as knowledge partner, Edges of Sri Lanka presents an evidence-based perspective on established strengths and evolving capabilities that contribute to Sri Lanka\u2019s competitiveness, resilience, and long-term growth. Together, the initiative complements the Expo\u2019s objective of reinforcing Sri Lanka\u2019s positioning under the theme \u201cIsland with Infinite Opportunities\u201d, aligning national narrative, market engagement, and investment promotion.\n\nSri Lanka Expo 2026 is positioned as the country\u2019s flagship international exhibition, aimed at showcasing Sri Lanka\u2019s export and investment potential while facilitating direct engagement with global buyers and investors through structured platforms such as business-to-business (B2B) meetings. The Expo seeks to strengthen Sri Lanka\u2019s standing as a competitive sourcing destination and create pathways for exporters and investors to form commercially viable partnerships.\n\nSpeaking at the launch, Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Minister Sunil Handunnetti emphasised the strategic intent behind the initiative: \u201cSri Lanka Expo 2026 is not just an event; it is a strategic platform for our exporters to reach new markets, attract international buyers, and showcase the best of Sri Lanka. It brings together our policies, our products, and our people to create real business opportunities in international markets.\u201d"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
