    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "d2887c126ad64d1277dbee516a04657c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1694,
    "chunk_text": "Speaking at the launch, Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Minister Sunil Handunnetti emphasised the strategic intent behind the initiative: \u201cSri Lanka Expo 2026 is not just an event; it is a strategic platform for our exporters to reach new markets, attract international buyers, and showcase the best of Sri Lanka. It brings together our policies, our products, and our people to create real business opportunities in international markets.\u201d\n\nWithin this framework, Edges of Sri Lanka plays a foundational role, complementing the Expo\u2019s engagement and deal-making function by providing international stakeholders with deeper context and insight. Through curated case studies, the initiative highlights Sri Lankan enterprises that demonstrate adaptive business models, innovation-led growth, and globally relevant capabilities rooted in local strengths.\n\nEDB Chairman and Chief Executive Officer Mangala Wijesinghe underscored the importance of this integrated approach:\n\n\u201cFor exporters, the Expo opens pathways to new markets and strategic partnerships. For international buyers and investors, Edges of Sri Lanka offers a clearer understanding of the quality, talent, and resilience that define Sri Lanka\u2019s business environment.\u201d\n\nDeloitte Country Managing Partner \u2013 Sri Lanka and Maldives Channa Manoharan said: \u201cEdges of Sri Lanka shines a light on a few of the country\u2019s distinctive strengths and emerging capabilities. By presenting credible, real-world business examples, the initiative helps investors and partners better understand Sri Lanka\u2019s value proposition, and supports more informed dialogue around investment, partnerships, and sustainable growth.\u201d"
  },
