    "description": "Sri Lanka Journalists for Global Justice condemns Khamenei killing, urges Govt. to do so",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/news/Sri-Lanka-Journalists-for-Global-Justice-condemns-Khamenei-killing-urges-Govt-to-do-so/56-789159",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1772757685.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-03-06-dailyftlk-7d384d50-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "e782b7021bd4b14e0a6c6ea1d06ee176",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1845,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka Journalists for Global Justice condemns Khamenei killing, urges Govt. to do so\n\nSri Lanka Journalists for Global Justice (SLJGJ) in a statement has strongly and unequivocally condemned the heinous assassination of Iran\u2019s Supreme Leader Ayatollah Khamenei by the US and Israel, and the unlawful war imposed on Iran in the midst of diplomatic efforts to find a solution to the dispute over Iran\u2019s nuclear program.\n\nThe Ayatollah was not only Iran\u2019s spiritual leader but a global icon against Western and Zionist imperialism, and hegemonic designs. This cowardly act, carried out as part of an illegal war in violation of the UN Charter and civilised norms, is utterly reprehensible. The killing of a revered leader of a nation with such a proud and ancient civilisation follows the recent kidnapping of Venezuela\u2019s democratically elected President and his wife by the US military. This blatant disregard for Venezuelan sovereignty and the killing of Iran\u2019s Supreme Leader show a disturbing and barbaric \u201cmight is right\u201d trend in world politics.\n\nEqually abominable is the failure of the international community to take effective action against such practices without confining their condemnation to empty words.\n\nWe are also deeply disturbed by the Sri Lankan Government\u2019s failure to condemn the assassination of Ayatollah Khamenei, a leader of a friendly nation that has supported us through thick and thin with military, economic, and diplomatic aid.\n\nWe urge the Government to condemn the killing of Ayatollah Khamenei and his family, as well as the barbaric bombing that killed more than 100 primary schoolgirls on the war\u2019s first day. Finally, we call on the Government to rise to the occasion, as true socialists would do, and issue an urgent call for peace and a resolution of the conflict through UN mechanisms."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
