    "description": "Foreign Minister offers condolences to Iran following death of Ayatollah Khamenei",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/news/Foreign-Minister-offers-condolences-to-Iran-following-death-of-Ayatollah-Khamenei/56-789160",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1772757776.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-03-06-dailyftlk-6cab5f5f-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "2fa97405eb6d93f5a5e9a53103b433b4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 925,
    "chunk_text": "Foreign Minister offers condolences to Iran following death of Ayatollah Khamenei\n\nForeign Affairs Minister Vijitha Herath on Wednesday visited the Embassy of the Islamic Republic of Iran in Colombo to convey condolences following the death of Iran\u2019s Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei.\n\nDuring the visit, the Foreign Minister expressed Sri Lanka\u2019s sympathies to the Government and people of Iran over the passing of the long-serving leader.\n\n\u201cToday, l offered my deepest condolences to the Islamic Republic of Iran on the death of His Eminence Ayatollah Ali Khamenei.\u201d\n\nIn a statement posted on the social media platform \u2018X,\u2019 Herath noted that relations between Sri Lanka and Iran had expanded during Khamenei\u2019s leadership.\n\n\u201cOur bilateral ties broadened significantly under his tenure. Sri Lanka remains appreciative of Iran\u2019s friendship. Our thoughts are with the Iranian people,\u201d the Minister said."
  },
  {
