    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "caef744de103eb2b91223f0109958584",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1593,
    "chunk_text": "Iran Embassy in Colombo condemns \u2018military aggression\u2019 by Israel and US\n\nThe Embassy of the Islamic Republic of Iran in Colombo has strongly condemned what it described as \u201csavage military aggression\u201d carried out by Israel and the US against Iran\u2019s sovereignty and territorial integrity.\n\nIn a statement issued on Monday, the Embassy alleged what it referred to as the \u201cZionist regime and US regime\u201d of committing an unlawful and provocative act in violation of international law and the Charter of the United Nations (UN).\n\n\u201cSuch hostile actions, particularly at a sensitive diplomatic juncture, once again reveal the true nature of these regimes and their disregard for peace, stability, and constructive dialogue,\u201d it added.\n\nReaffirming Tehran\u2019s position, the Embassy noted that the Islamic Republic of Iran reserved its inherent right to self-defence under Article 51 of the UN Charter. It stated that Iran\u2019s Armed Forces would deliver a \u201cdecisive response\u201d to any act of aggression in defence of the country\u2019s security, dignity and national interests.\n\nThe Embassy of the Islamic Republic of Iran in Colombo also called upon all freedom-loving and independent countries of the world to strongly condemn these attacks and to express their solidarity in support of the principles of national sovereignty, non-interference, and respect for international law.\n\n\u201cWhile remaining committed to the preservation of regional stability, the Islamic Republic of Iran will resolutely defend its national interests and the security of its people,\u201d the statement added."
  },
